      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2023 the Syndicate carried gross claims outstanding of GBP 3,045.2m. During 2023 there was a material gross reduction in prior year reserves of GBP 1,271.2m (a release of ~41.7% of opening gross reserves), primarily driven by the RiverStone reinsurance-to-close and quota share transactions which transferred discontinued 2018-and-prior (and certain 2019/2020) liabilities out of the Syndicate, together with favourable prior-year claims development and reinsurance recoveries. These RITC transactions materially distorted the primary statements and reduced gross technical liabilities, while the retained book also saw favourable development reflecting a benign claims year and reserve releases.",
